{"name":"Barako Brew","hex":"#4b2d2a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brew","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make tea or coffee by mixing tea leaves or coffee beans with hot water.","To heat wine, infusing it with spices; to mull."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The mixture formed by brewing; that which is brewed; a brewage, such as tea or beer.\n\n A serving of beer.","A serving of beer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brew"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kapeng barako","blocks":[{"text":"Kapeng barako, also known as Barako coffee or Batangas coffee, is a coffee varietal grown in the Philippines, particularly in the provinces of Batangas and Cavite. It belongs to the species Coffea liberica. The term is also used to refer to all coffee coming from those provinces. Barako in the languages of the Philippines means \"stud\" and is associated with the image of masculinity. Barako has a strong flavor and fragrance reminiscent of aniseed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Moon_Garden_%28Tagaytay%29_Kapeng_Barako.jpg/330px-Moon_Garden_%28Tagaytay%29_Kapeng_Barako.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kapeng_barako","wikidata":"Q263685"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Liberica_coffee_beans%2C_roasted.jpg/500px-Liberica_coffee_beans%2C_roasted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Liberica_coffee_beans%2C_roasted.jpg/500px-Liberica_coffee_beans%2C_roasted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Liberica beans from Mindoro, Philippines","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALiberica_coffee_beans%2C_roasted.jpg"}],"sounds":{"brew":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo